# License sidecars are compared byte-for-byte against the LF-normalized text
# embedded in the .embf binaries (test/embf-guard.test.js "bare-binary hole"
# guard) — core.autocrlf=true checkouts must not convert them to CRLF.
*.LICENSE.txt text eol=lf

# The memory index is loaded by Claude Code WHOLE, with a hard ceiling counted
# on the file as stored — a CR is a character (digitizer/tools/memory_budget.py).
# core.autocrlf=true Windows checkouts must not turn it into CRLF, which costs
# one extra character per line of ceiling (~146 of ~25,000 on 2026-10-26).
.claude/memory/*.md text eol=lf

# The outline-font starter set ships UNMODIFIED from google/fonts and
# tools/fetch_outline_fonts.py --check compares every TTF's sha256 with the
# registry's: a line-ending conversion would be a modification. The licence
# texts stay LF for the same reason the .LICENSE.txt sidecars do.
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
digitizer/digitizer_core/outline_fonts/**/OFL.txt text eol=lf

# Binary artifacts: never eol-convert or diff as text.
*.embf binary
*.png binary
*.onnx binary

# The calibrated judge's rubric is frozen by its sha256 (calibrated-judge/AMENDMENT-1.md);
# a CRLF checkout must not change the bytes a reader hashes.
docs/eye-pairs-2026-11-04/calibrated-judge/RUBRIC.md text eol=lf
